# 7b-3 (ticket OPUS-7B3-20260929-02; Q51: ordinary visibility is forward and down, a local is not visible outward):
# the bare name j after `end: for` -- j is declared in the for body, so outside the body it is not j at all, and the
# translator refuses it where it stands.  (The explicit path for\j is the place of declaration: unit_body_path_for.)
fn: mytest () int
    int: acc
    acc: 0
    for: int(i, 0) (i < 10) i++
        int: j i
        acc: j
    end: for
    return: j
end: mytest
int: r 0
r: mytest()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: r; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
